
{
  "content": "<p>This section contains lecture notes from the Fall 2000 version of the course. These notes can also be found in the <a href=\"../../video_galleries/video-lectures/index.html\">Video Lectures</a> section, under the Related Resources tab for each video. Demonstration handouts can be found there as well.</p>\n<p>Notes for Lecture 24 are not available.</p>\n<p><table>\n\n<thead>\n\n<tr>\n\n<th>\n\nLEC #\n</th>\n\n<th>\n\nTOPICS\n</th>\n\n<th>\n\nLECTURE NOTES\n</th>\n</p>\n</tr>\n\n<p></thead>\n\n<tr>\n\n<td>\n\n1\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\nIntroduction and lumped abstraction\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\n(<a href=\"../../resources/6002_l1/index.html\">PDF</a>)\n</td>\n</p>\n<p></tr>\n\n<tr>\n\n<td>\n\n2\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\nBasic circuit analysis method\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\n(<a href=\"../../resources/6002_l2/index.html\">PDF</a>)\n</td>\n</p>\n<p></tr>\n\n<tr>\n\n<td>\n\n3\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\nSuperposition, Thévenin and Norton\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\n(<a href=\"../../resources/6002_l3/index.html\">PDF</a>)\n</td>\n</p>\n<p></tr>\n\n<tr>\n\n<td>\n\n4\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\nThe digital abstraction\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\n(<a href=\"../../resources/6002_l4/index.html\">PDF</a>)\n</td>\n</p>\n<p></tr>\n\n<tr>\n\n<td>\n\n5\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\nInside the digital gate\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\n(<a href=\"../../resources/6002_l5/index.html\">PDF</a>)\n</td>\n</p>\n<p></tr>\n\n<tr>\n\n<td>\n\n6\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\nNonlinear analysis\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\n(<a href=\"../../resources/6002_l6/index.html\">PDF</a>)\n</td>\n</p>\n<p></tr>\n\n<tr>\n\n<td>\n\n7\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\nIncremental analysis\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\n(<a href=\"../../resources/6002_l7/index.html\">PDF</a>)\n</td>\n</p>\n<p></tr>\n\n<tr>\n\n<td>\n\n8\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\nDependent sources and amplifiers\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\n(<a href=\"../../resources/6002_l8/index.html\">PDF</a>)\n</td>\n</p>\n<p></tr>\n\n<tr>\n\n<td>\n\n9\n</td>\n\n<td>\n\nMOSFET amplifier large signal analysis\n</td>\n\n<td>\n</p>\n<p>(<a href=\"../../resources/6002_l9/index.html\">PDF</a>)</p>\n</td>\